    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀχθέω</span></b>  (pres. only in compd.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσ-οχθέω</span>, q. v.), fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					3.451
				</span></i>
			: 
				Ep.
			 Verb used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in aor.:—<i>to be sorely angered,
				vexed in spirit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤχθησαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.570
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				15.101
			</span></i>; elsewh. only in part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγ᾽ ὀχθήσας προσέφη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.517
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				4.30
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀχθήσας δ᾽ ἄρα εἶπε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.403
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀχθήσας προσεφώνεε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.182
				</span></i>
			.</div>
